	Porting to other platforms:

	This library was developed on an Amiga 3000, with the MIDI shared
library. I have, however, taken great pains to make it easy to port to just
about any other sane platform.
	All of the public routines ('eps*()') make no assumptions about how
MIDI data is sent back and forth between your computer and any EPSes attached
to it. They, in turn, make use of system-dependent routines hidden in a
subdirectory of their own. The directory 'libsrc/generic' contains a sample
system-dependent module with templates for all of the necessary routines.
Feel free to add new routines or modules, but keep them in a subdirectory.
	The other thing you need to modify is the "eps.h" include file,
specifically the declaration for 'struct EPSdesc'. At the top is a set of
#defines. Use the one appropriate for your architecture, or add a new one
if necessary.
	Following that is a set of system-dependent #includes. Add your own,
inside a "#ifdef ARCHITECTURE ... #endif" block.
	Much further down, you will find the declaration for "struct
EPSdesc". If you need to add any system-dependent fields, put them here,
inside a "#ifdef ARCHITECTURE ... #endif" block. This struct is not intended
to be portable, so go ahead and use ints and any other system-specific stuff
you like.
	That should be it. I've tried to make the Amiga-specific parts
separate and clearly marked. If I've made any incorrect assumptions as to
what is portable and what isn't, I'd like to hear about it. You can reach
me at arensb@kong.gsfc.nasa.gov .

